# Build enough to learn

A first prototype needs to answer a question. Choose the simplest version that lets you observe the behavior you care about.

## A simple example

A paper model can test a layout before you build the final object. Decide what the model can show and what it cannot show.

**Useful relationship:** model length = original length × scale

## Pause and try

Describe a small prototype and the single question it will answer.

